<meta seo title="Guides" description="Step-by-step BRAINLLM guides: build an app with a language model, turn compiler errors into fixes and make every page findable.">

<script>
  import { page } from 'brain:content'
  export async function load() {
    return page('guides', 1)
  }
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Guides</h1>
  <p>Each guide follows one BRAINLLM task from start to finish, with the commands you type and the output you get back,
    so you can repeat it on your own machine.</p>
  <p>Together they show how the framework is meant to be used: a language model writes the app, the compiler checks every
    file it writes and answers each mistake with the edit that fixes it, and the build publishes pages that people,
    search engines and AI assistants can read. Any diagnostic code they mention can be looked up with
    <code>brain explain</code>.</p>
  <p>They are written for two readers at once. If you are a developer, they explain what each step does and why the
    framework works that way. If you are handing the work to a model, every guide is also published as Markdown and
    listed in llms.txt, so the model reads the same instructions you do, without a browser.</p>
  <p>Each guide stands on its own. When a step needs more detail, it links to the reference: the
    <a href="/docs/cli">CLI and testing page</a> covers every command and the JSON error format, and the
    <a href="/docs">documentation</a> covers files, components, markup, styles, data and SEO one topic at a time. If a
    guide and the spec ever disagree, the spec wins: it is the only document that defines what an app can contain. New
    guides appear at the top of this list.</p>
  <ul class="entries">
    {#each props.entries as e (e.slug)}
      <li>
        <h2><a href={e.url}>{e.title}</a></h2>
        <p>{e.description}</p>
        {#if e.date}<time datetime={e.date}>{e.date}</time>{/if}
      </li>
    {/each}
  </ul>
  {#if props.next}<p><a href={props.next} rel="next">Older entries</a></p>{/if}
</main>

<style>
  .entries { display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  time { color: var(--muted); font-size: .875rem; }
</style>
